cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "pricecast: a parametric model of hourly electricity prices for prospective energy system studies"
abstract: >-
  Generates a full year of hourly day-ahead electricity prices in one shot from
  load, solar and wind generation, by a regression fitted on market years or on
  a scenario's hourly results, as an input to LP and MILP design studies.
  Because the model is parametric in its drivers and each year takes a fraction
  of a second, a scenario can be swept one driver at a time or its uncertain
  inputs sampled and propagated to a design. For a future year, a market-model
  scenario such as ENTSO-E's TYNDP 2026 supplies the drivers and the price
  level, and the model supplies the hourly shape. Ships models for five
  European bidding zones and the tools to build a future year: driver scaling,
  level matching with a floor, and two checks of the model's reach.
type: software
